n and wild-dog conservation science in a globally significant ecosystem, plus a 570-bird list","si":"deepdive","blurb":"Ruaha is a hub of lion and wild-dog conservation science in a globally significant ecosystem, plus a 570-bird list","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"DMC/specialist","wells":[],"wells_basis":"text supports no Well — needs a human read","si_all":["deepdive"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"primary","romance":"destination","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Jabali Ridge / Mwagusi honeymoon","si_tag":"ultra","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"~$900-2,500+/night all-in","timing":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","draw_rank":1,"hook":"Asilia''s Jabali Ridge tucked into a kopje above the plains, or Mwagusi''s legendary bush bandas on a sand river","si":"ultra","blurb":"Asilia''s Jabali Ridge tucked into a kopje above the plains, or Mwagusi''s legendary bush bandas on a sand river","when":"standing; peak 4-8 mo","commission":"consortia/Virtuoso + DMC","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance","safari","ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"evidenced","safari":"evidenced","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"A Ruaha wilderness honeymoon","si_tag":"romance","status":"live","tier":"luxury","price_band":"on application","timing":"Jun-Oct","draw_rank":1,"when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Jun-Oct","commission":"consortia/host","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"adventure":"destination","deepdive":"destination","romance":"primary","safari":"destination","ultra":"destination"},"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Ruaha?","a":"Not the parks - the advisory''s concerns are the far-southeastern Mtwara Region (terrorism, far away) and city petty crime, plus a flagged LGBTQ+ targeting concern travelers should weigh (Tanzanian law criminalizes same-sex relations). In Ruaha itself the risks are ordinary safari ones plus remoteness - it''s a fly-in wilderness, so carry AMREF evac + insurance and follow the walking-safari rules.","source":"newsweek.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why choose Ruaha over the northern circuit?","a":"For wildness and predators without the crowds - ~10% of the world''s lions in huge prides, one of the world''s best wild-dog populations, big elephant herds and a transition-zone game roster, all in Tanzania''s largest park with a fraction of the vehicles. It''s the connoisseur''s safari, best paired with Nyerere/Selous.","source":"national-parks.org","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Ruaha?","a":"The dry season, Jun-Oct, when the Great Ruaha River becomes the only water and game - lions, dogs, elephants - concentrates dramatically along it; the green season (Nov-Apr) is lush and superb for birds (570+ species) but some camps close and roads soften.","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"How do I get to Ruaha, and how long should I stay?","a":"Mostly by light-aircraft fly-in (from Dar, Iringa or as part of a southern-circuit hop); give it 3-4 nights to justify the flight and to do the river drives and a walking safari - it''s not a day-trip park.","source":"getsafaritours.com","si_tag":"safari"},{"q":"Do I need a visa or yellow-fever certificate for Tanzania?","a":"eVisa required - apply on the official portal before departure. Yellow fever is not required direct from the US/Europe, but is mandatory if you transit >12 h through a risk country like Kenya.","source":"tanzania-specialist.com","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Ruaha National Park Guide: Lions, Wild Dogs, Walking Safaris & Best Time","meta_description":"Plan a Ruaha safari - Tanzania''s largest, wildest and least-crowded park: ~10% of the world''s lions in record prides, one of the world''s best wild-dog populations, walking safaris and the Great Ruaha River - with the FCDO advisory, best time (Jun-Oct), the fly-in and where to stay on the southern circuit.","slug":"ruaha-tanzania","primary_keyword":"Ruaha National Park safari","long_tail":["Ruaha lions prides","Ruaha wild dogs","Ruaha walking safari","Ruaha vs Serengeti","is Tanzania safe safari","Ruaha best time to visit","southern circuit Tanzania"],"search_language":"sw","local_keywords":["Ruaha","simba","mbwa mwitu","tembo","mto"],"hreflang":["en","sw"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-08-01","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-01","last_verified_basis":"source_verified","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tanzania","read":"2026-08-20T14:54:17Z","source_updated":"2026-05-19T15:47:49+01:00"}]}},"booking":{"codes":["reconsider-travel","mtwara-terrorism-carveout-far","lgbtq-targeting"],"book_suppressed":false,"note":"also disclose the LGBTQ+ targeting consideration (same-sex relations criminalized). Travel with a licensed operator; remote fly-in - AMREF evac essential. Re-verify each cycle.","advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-08-01","hits":6,"misses":16,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; per the safari-build rule big game/predators is safari (PRIMARY here - lion + wild-dog stronghold), NOT globaladv; walking safar